's value — of an engine and of an outside-target span too — is held in process memory until the span closes and written only where the rule prints it; an event's line is unchanged, inside a span included. A named limit, read from the locked `tracing-subscriber 0.3.23` and not exercised: when a field formatter returns an error at span creation the layer itself `eprintln!`s the span's attributes with `Debug` to stderr, unscrubbed — the sink's field formatter writes into a `String` and returns no error (packages/escher-telemetry/src/lib.rs:102-116; packages/escher-telemetry/src/format.rs:138-177; packages/escher-telemetry/src/format.rs:200-250; as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-07-driver-command-spans/report.md). Its reach is that sink only: the upstream apps' `fmt::init()` stdout subscribers and the WPT runner's `env_logger` stay unscrubbed, the chained std panic hook still prints the raw panic message to stderr, and an allowlisted `log.file` can still carry a host path, now only for a bridged record under an engine target — the bridged third-party records that carried one at `RUST_LOG=info` (as measured at the chunk's smoke, escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-06-telemetry-bootstrap/report.md) are dropped whole (recorded by construction, not measured: a dropped record writes zero bytes, and `log.file` occurrences were not counted). Since 2026-10-07-sink-target-allowlist no record from a target outside the allowlist reaches stderr — stderr lines before → after the drop: the `escher-session` binary (the CRUD task, one `hello`, then `stop`) 0 → 0 at the default level, 1 → 1 at `info`, 1165 → 1 at `debug`, 1501 → 1 at `trace`; the windowed `seven_guis_native` (left on Home for 10 s, nobody clicks) 1 → 0, 3 → 1, 12,413 → 1, 47,482 → 1 — the one line left being the install line `INFO escher_telemetry`, with no stable id and no accessible name at any setting on either binary and stdout empty in all 16 readings; the cost is that a third-party WARN or ERROR no longer prints either — the windowed stand's one default-level line, `WARN winit_wayland::window::state`, is gone; typed text was first measured in process: `stand_act_spans` re-runs its test binary on two ignored children, each installing the sink with `init_with_writer` over an in-memory capture, and at `RUST_LOG=info` the capture of the six instance-level verbs and a refused call for each of the eight causes holds 0 occurrences of the three supplied texts (the typed text, the id naming no element, the unknown verb's text), 0 of 36 id needles and 0 of 8 name needles, in both layout modes; typed text in a sink-installing HOST's log is measured since 2026-10-10-driver-cli — the `escher-session` host runs the calls its socket's `call` request carries and writes one closed `command` span line per call run (`host_log`: 3 lines for 3 calls), and a typed sentinel occurs 0 times in that host's stderr at `RUST_LOG=trace`, with 0 id needles and 0 name needles, under both builds (`host_log` as `-p seven_guis` and as `--workspace`); by level, on a snapshot · click · type flow, the host built alone writes 0 lines unset and 4 at `info`, `debug` and `trace` (three command spans and the install line), and the workspace-built host one engine line more, `blitz_dom::document` at INFO, with 0 sentinel occurrences, 0 of 15 ids and 0 of 6 names at every level and stdout 0 B (as measured at escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-10-driver-cli/evidence/by-level.md) — re-read at 2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep: the workspace-built host now prints that `focussed node` line twice, 6 lines / 978 B where it read 5 / 860 B, the host built alone unchanged at 4 / 742 B, needles 0 (escher-0.1.0/chunks/2026-10-14-stand-requirement-sweep/evidence/log-counts.md); since 2026-10-10-mcp-surface the sink also prints a second `escher_driver` span, `tool_call`, one closed line per MCP `tools/call`, holding `tool` (the table's word, absent for an unknown tool) and `ending` (`accepted` · `refused` · `error`) only, the parent of `